<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><description>Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 20:20:25 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Truth or Fake</category><title>Meet 'America': Trump’s AI chatbot changes answers after challenging his claims</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/meet-america-trump-s-ai-chatbot-changes-answers-after-challenging-his-claims-1</link><description>
Donald Trump has launched “America”, an AI chatbot designed as a digital portal for US government information. But its responses appear to be changing. The chatbot initially challenged several of Trump’s claims, including on the 2020 election and inflation, providing evidence and links. More recently, it has refused to answer some of the same questions. Other responses still contradict Trump, while some echo his views. Vedika Bahl tests the chatbot, and its varying answers in Truth or Fake.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2e053cc0-bd06-11f1-b6c3-7be0f5469a6a/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-9934752996abd64a62a23a7-71615901.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2e053cc0-bd06-11f1-b6c3-7be0f5469a6a/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-9934752996abd64a62a23a7-71615901.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8a1d163c-bd05-11f1-a25d-039addfcfd17</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 20:08:13 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Vedika BAHL</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'Hard to see Man City getting anything other than the book thrown at them', expert says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/hard-to-see-man-city-getting-anything-other-than-the-book-thrown-at-them-expert-says</link><description>
Manchester City enjoyed a meteoric rise from mid-table mediocrity to Premier League domination, but their golden era could be forever tarnished after they were found guilty of scores of financial rule breaches. FRANCE 24's Mark Owen speaks with James Reade, Professor of Economics at the University of Reading. He says that it's unlikely that the club will see any leniency from football authorities: "it's hard to see it getting anything other than the book thrown at them".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a89e3c52-bd06-11f1-9418-1b050e7dec5f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260930-210843-212132-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a89e3c52-bd06-11f1-9418-1b050e7dec5f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260930-210843-212132-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ae3f44f8-bd06-11f1-ba91-3f96bfe93f95</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 19:56:07 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sport</category><title>Ronaldo leaves Portugal training camp after coach drops him from upcoming match</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/sport/20260930-ronaldo-leaves-portugal-training-camp-after-coach-drops-him-from-upcoming-match</link><description>
Portugal captain and striker Cristiano Ronaldo said Wednesday he had walked out on the national team's training camp in Copenhagen after coach Jorge Jesus announced the 41-year-old player would be dropped from the team's next match against Denmark.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a94802c6-bcf9-11f1-ab0c-ddce071186a9/w:1024/p:16x9/5e59e151fd9de4028ee658699a78fdd885897e2d.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a94802c6-bcf9-11f1-ab0c-ddce071186a9/w:1024/p:16x9/5e59e151fd9de4028ee658699a78fdd885897e2d.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2b7df058-bd03-11f1-93e6-291217637f3c</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 19:14:33 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a94802c6-bcf9-11f1-ab0c-ddce071186a9/w:1024/p:16x9/5e59e151fd9de4028ee658699a78fdd885897e2d.jpg">© Liselotte Sabroe, Ritzau Scanpix via AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Clashes between French teens, police as school blockades intensify</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/clashes-between-french-teens-police-as-school-blockades-intensify</link><description>
French teenagers on Tuesday set fire to rubbish bins and threw projectiles at police who responded with batons and tear gas, with hundreds detained across the country over the blockades and protests demanding better conditions at schools. Since last week, students have staged protests outside hundreds of schools over grievances including timetables, class sizes and a shortage of teachers as well as overheated classrooms during this year's heatwaves. FRANCE 24's Rachel Griffiths reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5b148b08-bd01-11f1-ac56-1b050e7dec5f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260930-204115-204316-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5b148b08-bd01-11f1-ac56-1b050e7dec5f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260930-204115-204316-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">600a7cb2-bd01-11f1-9948-af42048694dc</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 19:07:32 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The Debate</category><title>Ethiopia back to civil war? Horn of Africa fears spillover effect of renewed fighting</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260930-ethiopia-back-to-civil-war-horn-of-africa-fears-spillover-effect-of-renewed-fighting</link><description>
After contagion in the Arabian Peninsula, should the entire Horn of Africa fear a domino effect? Just as Donald Trump’s decision to invade Iran drew the Saudis back to Yemen: did threats over the Strait of Bab el-Mandeb light the fuse in Ethiopia, where last week, unresolved issues between the government and its Tigray region erupted? Could a potential return to civil war draw in regional rivals?
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b4b4ab32-b81c-11f1-9a75-9d4ae5c4ba17/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-24T101012Z-919341318-RC2KPNA74E5F-RTRMADP-3-ETHIOPIA-SECURITY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b4b4ab32-b81c-11f1-9a75-9d4ae5c4ba17/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-24T101012Z-919341318-RC2KPNA74E5F-RTRMADP-3-ETHIOPIA-SECURITY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">57fa248a-bcf9-11f1-9678-0d99ded520a3</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 19:04:20 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>British PM alleges there are 'strong indications' Iran was involved in Fairford airbase incident</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260930-british-pm-alleges-there-are-strong-indications-iran-was-involved-in-fairford-airbase-incident</link><description>
UK Prime Minister Andy Burnham on Wednesday insisted that there were "strong indications" that Tehran was involved in a security incident on Sunday near an airbase in England that the US military uses in its war against Iran. The British government has still not explained the nature of the incident – in which five British men were arrested only to be later released on bail – and no explosives were found at the scene. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/79072c1c-bc0a-11f1-9add-555a0aff87a4/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-29T064654Z-1635109463-RC2USNAUC1I4-RTRMADP-3-BRITAIN-USA-FAIRFORD.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/79072c1c-bc0a-11f1-9add-555a0aff87a4/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-29T064654Z-1635109463-RC2USNAUC1I4-RTRMADP-3-BRITAIN-USA-FAIRFORD.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">deb4a9b0-bcfd-11f1-9520-4f451fb619c5</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 19:01:30 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/79072c1c-bc0a-11f1-9add-555a0aff87a4/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-29T064654Z-1635109463-RC2USNAUC1I4-RTRMADP-3-BRITAIN-USA-FAIRFORD.jpg">© Toby Shepheard, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>UK-France 'one in, one out' migrant exchange deal is scrapped</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260930-uk-france-one-in-one-out-migrant-exchange-deal-is-scrapped</link><description>
A British-French agreement aimed at reducing the number of people trying to cross the English Channel in small boats has been scrapped, London said Wednesday. The pilot programme was intended to break the business model of "people smugglers" by exchanging undocumented migrants who had made the crossing for people who legally applied for asylum.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/97e2e0e8-bced-11f1-9d0b-d367a0468893/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26271435063936.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/97e2e0e8-bced-11f1-9d0b-d367a0468893/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26271435063936.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">56bf2f9a-bced-11f1-8b23-5bbf84ef822f</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 17:12:12 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/97e2e0e8-bced-11f1-9d0b-d367a0468893/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26271435063936.jpg">© Jean-François Badias, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>France to unveil 2027 budget as debt hits record high</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260930-france-to-unveil-2027-budget-as-debt-hits-record-high</link><description>
As the French government prepares to unveil its latest budget, the country's debt is at a record high and growing every day. France's public debt currently stands at nearly 3.6 trillion euros, nearly 60 billion of that added in the last three months alone.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a9b15182-bce4-11f1-bb0a-ddce071186a9/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260930-152848-153036-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a9b15182-bce4-11f1-bb0a-ddce071186a9/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260930-152848-153036-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">aefa6908-bce4-11f1-a1f2-bb769a31d620</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 16:58:35 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Israel PM says pilot of rerouted flight tried to crash plane</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260930-israel-pm-says-pilot-of-rerouted-flight-tried-to-crash-plane</link><description>
Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said Wednesday that the pilot of a Tel Aviv-bound flydubai flight had tried to crash the plane and kill its passengers, after the aircraft was forced to make an emergency landing in Saudi Arabia. Passengers gave a similar account of the incident on board, describing a fight for control after the plane suddenly plummeted, losing around 17,000 feet of altitude in the span of a minute, according to the Flightradar24 website.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b3e4ddf4-bce4-11f1-8ae7-d367a0468893/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260930-160148-160351-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b3e4ddf4-bce4-11f1-8ae7-d367a0468893/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260930-160148-160351-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bd38ca64-bce4-11f1-bd55-47dfdf5015ff</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 16:57:41 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>New York Gov pushes for probe into Cornell's handling of gang rape allegation</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260930-new-york-gov-pushes-for-probe-into-cornell-s-handling-of-gang-rape-allegation</link><description>
New York Gov. Kathy Hochul on Tuesday called for an investigation into Cornell University's response to a 2024 gang rape allegation in which a woman says she was sexually assaulted by seven students after being plied with alcohol and drugs. It comes as prosecutors reopen an investigation into the alleged rape following claims the elite college failed to properly punish the men involved.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b83cc204-bce4-11f1-89b4-d367a0468893/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260930-171246-171433-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b83cc204-bce4-11f1-89b4-d367a0468893/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260930-171246-171433-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bda5f3b4-bce4-11f1-afb8-c55a6dd55169</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 16:55:36 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Climate change reshaping the polar oceans, says report</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260930-climate-change-reshaping-the-polar-oceans-says-report</link><description>
Climate change is increasingly reshaping the polar oceans, with Arctic waters warming rapidly, sea ice shrinking and wildlife losing habitat at both ends of the planet, an annual report said Wednesday. The Copernicus Ocean State Report depicts profound changes across the world's seas, from record-breaking heatwaves in the Mediterranean and Black seas to shifts in marine ecosystems and increasingly acidic waters.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7ae5d166-bce4-11f1-b4bb-ddce071186a9/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260930-154103-154250-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7ae5d166-bce4-11f1-b4bb-ddce071186a9/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260930-154103-154250-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8204f1de-bce4-11f1-9e65-e5d622dd5f24</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 16:53:09 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Syria: An exclusive look at the integration of Uyghur fighters in armed forces</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260930-syria-an-exclusive-look-at-the-integration-of-uyghur-fighters-in-armed-forces</link><description>
Several factions of foreign fighters are credited with helping topple Syria's Bashar al-Assad nearly two years ago - among them, the Uyghurs, a predominantly Muslim, Turkic ethnic minority spread across Central Asia - notably in China's Xinjiang region. They eventually became amongst the largest contingents of foreign fighters in Syria, though those who have stayed and built lives there are notoriously secretive. However, France 24's Wassim Nasr was recently in Syria and had exclusive access to Uyghur fighters there.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/553bc02e-bce4-11f1-9888-098db7fa8bc7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260930-152118-152816-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/553bc02e-bce4-11f1-9888-098db7fa8bc7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260930-152118-152816-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5a81a6ca-bce4-11f1-9219-f5c151cdc8c4</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 16:45:19 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>‘Attempted terror attack’: What happened on board the rerouted Flydubai flight?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260930-attempted-terror-attack-what-happened-on-board-the-rerouted-flydubai-flight</link><description>
The co-pilot of a flight from Dubai to Tel Aviv ​tried ‌to crash the plane after stabbing the pilot, but passengers then ⁠held him down while other pilots landed the plane safely in Saudi Arabia, Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said ‌on Wednesday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b44a2bda-bce6-11f1-9437-098db7fa8bc7/w:1024/p:16x9/mini3-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b44a2bda-bce6-11f1-9437-098db7fa8bc7/w:1024/p:16x9/mini3-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c62e1938-bce6-11f1-a15d-718e41bf9f8a</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 16:04:30 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Appeals court halts execution of Tennessee woman less than two hours before lethal injection</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260930-appeals-court-halts-execution-of-tennessee-woman-less-than-two-hours-before-lethal-injection</link><description>
A US appeals court ordered a "short stay of execution" for death row inmate Christa Pike, less than two hours before she was scheduled to be the first woman put to death in the state in more than two centuries. The court halted the execution to give it time to consider Pike's claims that her history of severe sexual abuse had not been taken into consideration during sentencing.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7a4f7cc8-bce1-11f1-a0fb-1b050e7dec5f/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-30T135639Z-1416470123-RC2PTNAYXSRM-RTRMADP-3-TENNESSEE-EXECUTION.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7a4f7cc8-bce1-11f1-a0fb-1b050e7dec5f/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-30T135639Z-1416470123-RC2PTNAYXSRM-RTRMADP-3-TENNESSEE-EXECUTION.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">35ef9c0c-bce1-11f1-bb71-759a78fd8c13</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 16:03:32 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7a4f7cc8-bce1-11f1-a0fb-1b050e7dec5f/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-30T135639Z-1416470123-RC2PTNAYXSRM-RTRMADP-3-TENNESSEE-EXECUTION.jpg">© J. Miles Cary, USA Today Network via Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Russia ramps up disinformation attacks on French media ahead of 2027 Presidential race</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260930-russia-ramps-up-disinformation-attacks-on-french-media-ahead-of-2027-presidential-race</link><description>
Pro-Russian influence operations have caused a surge of 850% in fake news stories mimicking real media brands, according to a report published this week by disinformation specialist, NewsGuard. Out of the 15 most imitated news outlets, eight are French – including FRANCE 24.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a036fb0c-b8f7-11f1-8a9f-555a0aff87a4/w:1024/p:16x9/Main-Russie-Hackers.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a036fb0c-b8f7-11f1-8a9f-555a0aff87a4/w:1024/p:16x9/Main-Russie-Hackers.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d0aa5a9e-bcd1-11f1-b26a-9d70296f33be</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 15:29:40 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a036fb0c-b8f7-11f1-8a9f-555a0aff87a4/w:1024/p:16x9/Main-Russie-Hackers.png">© France 24 graphics studio</source><dc:creator>Grégoire SAUVAGE</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Prosecutor reopens probe into Cornell gang rape allegations</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260930-prosecutor-reopens-probe-into-cornell-gang-rape-allegations</link><description>
A New York prosecutor has reopened an investigation into gang rape allegations at a Cornell University fraternity in response to a lawsuit filed by a woman who says she was sexually assaulted in 2024 by seven students after being plied with alcohol and drugs. Tompkins County District Attorney Matthew Van Houten said Monday that his office will present evidence to a grand jury as he faces questions from the public about why there were no criminal prosecutions in the case. France 24's Annette Young, host of The 51 %, has more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a4c0d3ea-bcd1-11f1-bde5-816a8398162d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260930-143905-144333-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a4c0d3ea-bcd1-11f1-bde5-816a8398162d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260930-143905-144333-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a9dab044-bcd1-11f1-803d-291ff30a4b14</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 15:06:20 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Macron says UK’s return to EU would be ‘excellent news’</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260930-replay-france-s-macron-calls-for-stronger-europe-on-spain-trip</link><description>
Speaking alongside Spanish Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez on Wednesday, French President Emmanuel Macron said that it would be "a good decision" if the UK decided to rejoin the European Union. The two leaders met at the Moncloa Palace in Madrid on the second day of Macron's two-day state visit to Spain.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f943f80e-bcc5-11f1-9e59-d367a0468893/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-30T115111Z-1926653752-RC2NTNAIQ2O3-RTRMADP-3-SPAIN-FRANCE-POLITICS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f943f80e-bcc5-11f1-9e59-d367a0468893/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-30T115111Z-1926653752-RC2NTNAIQ2O3-RTRMADP-3-SPAIN-FRANCE-POLITICS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">984b155e-bcd0-11f1-a510-03c796665186</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 15:01:32 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>arts24</category><title>Tom Cruise's 'Digger' divides critics as Zurich Film Festival stars steal the spotlight</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20260930-tom-cruise-s-digger-divides-critics-as-zurich-film-festival-stars-steal-the-spotlight</link><description>
This week on arts24's film show, an unrecognisable Tom Cruise takes a career gamble in "Digger", Alejandro González Iñárritu’s new satire, in which he plays an oil billionaire whose company initiates a world-ending ecological disaster. Critics are divided, but is an Oscar nomination possible? Also in cinemas this week, Anne Hathaway and Dakota Johnson star in the latest Colleen Hoover adaptation, "Verity".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3770b5a6-bcdd-11f1-8053-816a8398162d/w:1024/p:16x9/DLS-AFF-DIGGER-frame-49.jpeg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3770b5a6-bcdd-11f1-8053-816a8398162d/w:1024/p:16x9/DLS-AFF-DIGGER-frame-49.jpeg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2dd88a40-bcb6-11f1-a291-25662a7778f4</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 14:47:46 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Charlotte Lam</dc:creator></item><item><category>Entre Nous</category><title>What if art could help you live longer?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20260930-what-if-art-could-help-you-live-longer</link><description>
In this episode of Entre Nous, Delano D'Souza speaks to Daisy Fancourt, professor at University College London and a leading researcher on how the arts affects our brains and bodies. In her book "Art Cure" she draws on scientific evidence to show how the arts can transform our health and what her research suggests we should be doing to optimise the benefits.
